| `transports.serve.memory_cap_mb` | integer or null | `4096` | a whole number, 1 or more, or null | `scripts/resource_limits.py` (`serve_limits`, `cap_memory`) for `api/rest_fastapi/serve.py`, `mcp/protocol.py` (`run_stdio_server`) and `api/grpc/server.py` (`serve`) | Sets the mebibytes (MiB) of address space (RLIMIT_AS) a server process may hold before an allocation past it is a MemoryError; null sets no cap, and a platform without setrlimit runs uncapped and says so on stderr. It does not cover a file in a memory-backed directory such as `/dev/shm`, the total of the processes the server starts (each inherits its own copy of the cap), or resident memory, which address space overstates. Absent, the server writes `[using default] transports.serve.memory_cap_mb = 4096` to stderr. | a model child's time: `models.timeout_seconds` | always |
